.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
# ...and its backups. A .env.bak sitting beside it is the same secrets
# under a name the single-file pattern did not match.
.env.*
!.env.example
# data/ is ignored whole, not file by file. Two reasons, and the second is the
# one that bites: the store is a large binary that changes wholesale on every
# write and holds the user records, and on the runner `data/` is a *symlink* to
# the mounted volume. Git cannot check a tracked file out through a symlinked
# directory — it deletes the symlink and puts a real directory there instead.
# That silently splits the deployment in two: the API writes ROOT-relative to
# the new empty directory while every loader still writes the volume. Tracking
# anything under data/ is what causes it, so nothing under data/ is tracked.
/data/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# Claude Code local worktrees and session scratch
.claude/
.pytest_cache/

# Built by `atlas dataset`. The explorer reads the API directly now, so this
# is an optional export rather than something the page depends on — and a
# committed copy is wrong by default between pipeline runs.
src/frontend/public/data/

